      "reasons": [
        "The definition states that statistical process control detects “meaningful changes in a process,” but the packet specifically describes it (via run charts and Anhøj rules) as useful for detecting “persistent shifts,” without asserting the broader claim about detecting “meaningful changes.”",
        "Aside from the contested generalization, the rest of the definition (data over time, charts/runs charts, persistent shifts, long runs on one side of the centre line, and crossings of the centre) is supported by the packet."
